    "Nonconvergence in braking or any evaluated action withdraws to zero targets, retries next interval and disqualifies recovery or progress.",
    "Upright stance also receives braking reserves and feasibility checks; pure planning and atomic commit preserve state on refusal.",
    "Independent full replay binds all selected commands, reserve estimates, feasibility decisions, fallback and current native force limits.",
    "Zero-world refusal controls cover all-infeasible and nonconvergent withdrawals. Native route covers active command reserves, recurring fresh checks, held patterns and upright stance; it reports any observed fallback without claiming every refusal occurs in a native world.",
